 "reading": "ProjectionState lives in memory on the agent. The gate declines a FRESH pass when the request replays signed thinking on native Messages or Converse. After a restart every row archived earlier counts as fresh again, so with the gate those rows go out in full under a block that was signed over their stubs: the gate undoes archived rows. The plain carrier re-projects on that request; whether it invalidates the block then depends on whether the re-projection also archives rows that were not stubbed before (end-to-end run: yes, one row; direct call: no). Without a restart, the gate keeps every archived row and invalidates nothing.",
 "paths_into_it": {
  "run_end_to_end": "thinking turned on mid-session (CLI /reasoning retires the agent; the first request after that has no signed thinking yet, so the re-projection goes through) followed by a SessionDB resume",
  "run_by_direct_call": "an in-place route switch from chat completions to native Messages (as /model or a fallback round trip would do), followed by a new agent",
  "not_run": "the real /model and fallback-provider code paths; a gateway agent rebuild (editing any of the four projection keys rebuilds it) and a process restart are modelled by the new agent"
 },
 "denominators": {
  "cells": 24,
  "errored_scored_zero": 0,
  "infra_excluded": 0,
  "completeness": 1.0,
  "note": "end to end: 3 arms x 2 modes x 3 reps; direct call: 2 arms x 3 reps"
 },
