 "verdict": "KEEP (gate defect): with gate v4 (= v3 code), 4 of 4 archived rows go out in full on the first request after the resume and 1 thinking block is replayed over a rewritten prefix; without the resume 0. The plain carrier re-stubs 7 of 7 byte-identically but archives 1 more row, which invalidates 1 block on that request. Direct call (route switch): v4 sends 9 of 9 archived rows in full and the latest signed block's prefix changes; the carrier re-stubs all 9 identically and the prefix is unchanged.",
 "supersedes": null
}
